 \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"652f7e2c4a165267d1f1ccddb1ac4396cfaa5ff0ea8dbe5f2e2385c3d7618d6e","event_uuid":"df98ab10-346d-4f63-b8b6-33c9216f00c5","position":{"commit_sha":"7b1f72965ce3fa2977c6912dadafbd2bc1b257e5","position":"1788089297345186001-df98ab10-346d-4f63-b8b6-33c9216f00c5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d225922c0da5c077496adcdf7c284d58929bd514a67499526d52976d6110767e","event_uuid":"a742b0cd-2c4e-42f7-b8bc-1c4da0bb8915","position":{"commit_sha":"5cf6c2955731739ca4b8291cf041376be4e21a89","position":"1788089465379434754-a742b0cd-2c4e-42f7-b8bc-1c4da0bb8915"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9966230f783e467597bc82af99ea20dddc520a21c9c9657b0cb9fc0d0759a2df","event_uuid":"730c69ea-ec97-451b-b04b-4965d80810d6","position":{"commit_sha":"5cf6c2955731739ca4b8291cf041376be4e21a89","position":"1788089465396322048-730c69ea-ec97-451b-b04b-4965d80810d6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029128934029385,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"56aa875d-2ccd-4c78-8e5c-5e06fa65f12c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4bd8-a2bb-813b-427e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `pass3_over_findings`) is deterministic; every input is in the v2 sidecar (`sidecar.py:702-703` persists per-finding `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` losslessly). `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` proves the replay works but is a one-off script with hardcoded baselines.\n\n`orchestrator.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, *, execution_review=False)` (`orchestrator.py:662-711`) is the REAL LIVE path: `_threshold_for` special-cases `\"prerequisite-consistency\" -> (0.60, True)`, else resolves live via `_criteria.threshold_for(criteria, crit_by_id, gate=\"plan_review\")`, bumps `block_threshold = max(bt, 0.80)` when `execution_review and blocking_enabled` (`orchestrator.py:687-688`); applies `_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` under `if execution_review:` (line 698) before delegating.\n\n**`execution_review` recovery — exact call.** `sidecar.parse_review_phase_metadata(payload)` (`payload` = the WHOLE sidecar data Mapping, per `sidecar.py:541-556`) returns `{\"phase\": \"planning\"|\"execution\", \"priority_floor\": ...}` (raises `SidecarReviewPhaseError` on a malformed payload). Per `resign.py:280-286`'s real usage: `phase_metadata = sidecar.parse_review_phase_metadata(data); execution_review = phase_metadata[\"phase\"] == \"execution\"` — guard `SidecarReviewPhaseError` with a `\"planning\"` default. It is NOT a persisted per-finding field, and threaded into BOTH `pass3_decide` (for `replayed-stored`) and `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` (for `live-baseline`).\n\n**Registry drift is distinct from `impact_model_version`.** Thresholds live in `criteria_routing.json`, governed by `regver`. Tier-0 computes THREE things per finding:\n1. **stored** — the sidecar's decision.\n2. **replayed-stored** — `pass3_decide` fed the PERSISTED `block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` + recovered `execution_review` (no threshold re-resolution) — harness self-check; MUST always equal `stored`.\n3. **live-baseline** — `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` (live-resolved, same `execution_review`) — may legitimately differ from `stored` on registry drift.\n\n**Candidate** (`--candidate <name>`) is diffed against **live-baseline**. Resolved via `candidates/__init__.py`'s `CANDIDATES: dict[str, Candidate]` (`overlay: dict[str, tuple[float, bool]]`, `impact_fn: Callable = review_kernel.impact_plan`). `\"current\"` is built-in (empty overlay). Candidate's `threshold_for` mirrors `_threshold_for` against the overlay; `_restrict_on_target_veto_to_grounded` applied identically; then `review_kernel.pass3_over_findings(..., threshold_for=<mirrored>, impact_fn=<candidate's>, execution_review=...)`.\n\n`corpus.build_corpus`'s cache rows are summary-only; `findings`/`verification`/the sidecar payload need the SAME re-read `labels.py` uses: `_enumerate_event_blobs` + `_batch_cat` matched by `review_event_uuid`.\n\n**Plan-v4->v5 baseline — full dependency set.** `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` defines, in order: `import re` (23), `UNDECOMPOSED_RULES` (37-65), `DOD_RULES` (67-113), `ADVISORY_KIND`/`FLOOR_KINDS` (115-123), `RULES` (124), `classify` (127-161), `legacy_impact_plan` (162-191); `rescore` (192+) stays in the doc script. ALL of the former move verbatim into a NEW `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py`; `plan_v5_rescore.py` imports them from there.\n\n**Label-proxy metrics, enumerated.** When `labels_path` supplied: (a) `blocking_agreement_rate` = fraction of scored TICKETS where the candidate's PASS/BLOCK verdict matches `labels.escape_signals`' outcome (candidate BLOCK <-> an escaped/failed ticket; candidate PASS <-> clean_close); (b) `proxy_precision` = TP/(TP+FP) and `proxy_recall` = TP/(TP+FN) over that same 2x2, treating candidate-BLOCK-predicts-escape as positive; (c) `coverage_fraction` = tickets with a usable label / tickets in the corpus. ELSE: report states these are not computed.\n\n**Friction rate**: `count(findings where live-baseline is non-blocking AND candidate is blocking) / count(all findings scored)`. \"Relief count\" (reverse direction) reported separately.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (+ `legacy_v4_baseline.py`, `candidates/__init__.py`, `report.py`, `__main__.py`):\n\n- Move `import re`, `UNDECOMPOSED_RULES`, `DOD_RULES`, `ADVISORY_KIND`, `FLOOR_KINDS`, `RULES`, `classify`, `legacy_impact_plan` into `legacy_v4_baseline.py`; `plan_v5_rescore.py` imports them, keeps `rescore`.\n- Input: corpus, OPTIONAL `labels_path`, `--candidate <name>` via `candidates.CANDIDATES[name]`.\n- Full-body re-read per row; recover `execution_review` via `sidecar.parse_review_phase_metadata(data)[\"phase\"] == \"execution\"` (guard `SidecarReviewPhaseError` -> `\"planning\"`); `data[\"findings\"]` + per-index persisted thresholds + `verification` feed Pass-3.\n- `__main__.py`: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate <name> [--labels <path>]`.\n- Per finding compute `stored`, `replayed-stored`, `live-baseline`, `candidate`.\n- AC2: `legacy_v4_baseline.classify`/`RULES` mapping vs `legacy_v4_baseline.legacy_impact_plan`.\n- Report: flip matrix — (a) `stored` vs `live-baseline` = registry-drift, (b) `live-baseline` vs `candidate` = candidate-induced (primary); friction rate + relief count; per-criterion deltas; priority shift. IF `labels_path`: `blocking_agreement_rate`/`proxy_precision`/`proxy_recall`/`coverage_fraction`; ELSE not computed.\n- Post-verdict floors replayed only when inputs present.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/legacy_v4_baseline.py` (new — relocated from `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py`)\n- `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` (edited — imports from the new module)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/candidates/__init__.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: `replayed-stored` exactly equals `stored` for every fixture finding INCLUDING an execution-phase row with a `veto:plan-goal-satisfied` drop and a row at the 0.80 bump; a fixture with a malformed `review_phase` payload defaults to planning without crashing; a registry threshold differing from persisted shows `live-baseline` != `stored` while `replayed-stored` still == `stored`; candidate `\"current\"` == `live-baseline`; overlay flips boundary findings; friction rate + relief count on a known-ratio fixture; label-proxy metrics (all four) computed correctly against a fixture with known labels; unknown `--candidate` raises a clear error; v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` skipped; pre-v5 row classified via `legacy_v4_baseline.classify` vs `legacy_impact_plan`; `plan_v5_rescore.py` still runs post-extraction; label-proxy metrics omitted without `labels_path`; `__main__.py` dispatch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero `replayed-stored` vs `stored` mismatches, including execution-phase rows; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4->plan-v5 change (via `legacy_v4_baseline`) reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report separately states registry-drift flips and candidate-induced flips, plus friction rate and per-criterion deltas; checked by inspection.\n- [ ] IF a labels file is supplied, the report additionally contains `blocking_agreement_rate`, `proxy_precision`, `proxy_recall`, and `coverage_fraction`; checked by inspection when available.\n- [ ] The Pass-3 replay itself (excluding any optional label-proxy step) completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop over the real corpus, with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and no provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py","reason":"Pass-3 replay"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py","reason":"diff report"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py","reason":"module entry point"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"generated reports"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","4bd8-a2bb-813b-427e"],["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"a742b0cd-2c4e-42f7-b8bc-1c4da0bb8915","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["plan-review","evals","tier-0","pass-3"],"ticket_id":"5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb","ticket_type":"story","title":"Tier-0 harness: replay Pass-3 calculation, thresholds and routing overlays over the whole corpus (zero LLM)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["256b1be8-db50-45d5-b826-5366b0154324","2501382b-0689-4e18-bcc9-34036a53ab1a","dc73459c-6efd-4243-b056-70380f2415e7","5818a323-7c6f-4553-b968-e9c80983034c","a8570737-5855-4d22-a33e-ccb73280144d","9f1f1655-3fd8-42fc-8104-f9377865e730","d7d0502f-7ec6-4124-abab-5c5f3add6204","7c06cac0-7d8d-44de-b0c3-12ede3629cf0","bd0ed9ee-0ab2-4aee-abab-7ff21ff7c414","17070043-ef90-4fe3-a91a-91ec358bc493","242960a4-0cf0-4981-97f6-28dae169aa04","61b894f5-bd8b-4ff6-95d2-44d10f472675","df98ab10-346d-4f63-b8b6-33c9216f00c5","a742b0cd-2c4e-42f7-b8bc-1c4da0bb8915","730c69ea-ec97-451b-b04b-4965d80810d6"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788089465396322049,"uuid":"5a3155c7-ba57-46da-bd42-171100e4de37"}